  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 1402.03 Safety Factors",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 1402.03 Safety Factors. All consideration for public safety shall be given in designating the location of each carnival or amusement ride and the safe installation thereof, including but not limited to the following:\n\n(a) The physical nature of surrounding objects or surfaces that might produce undesirable contact for the riders of the carnival or ride;\n\n(b) The reasonably foreseeable changes that are likely to occur in the location or nature of the surroundings, such as flooding;\n\n(c) The site shall be free from large rocks, debris, or any holes; and\n\n(d) The site shall be sufficiently level to provide safe operation of the ride or device.\n\nSource. #2229, eff 12-31-82; ss by #2950, eff 1-3-85; ss by #4531, eff 1-1-89; ss by #5940, INTERIM, eff 1-1-95; ss by #5952, eff 1-24-95, EXPIRED: 1-24-03\n\nNew. #7833, INTERIM, eff 2-22-03, EXPIRED: 8-21-03\n\nNew. #8045, eff 2-20-04; amd by #8319, EMERGENCY, eff 4-5-05, EXPIRED: 10-2-05; amd by #8649, eff 6-2-06; ss by #10131, eff 5-18-12; amd by #12615, eff 8-28-18; ss by #13535, INTERIM, eff 1-25-23; ss by #13666, eff 6-20-23; ss by #14139, eff 11-28-24, EXPIRES: 11-28-34) (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Saf-C 1400)",
